      {
        "id": 77135,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-14T23:45:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I definitely wouldn’t say they aren’t worthwhile,  Omni-Cannon is significanlty better at takking out a target with DR or killing a high hp target the round it comes into play. However, even so, that is only the end game (possibly), there are tons of decisions before then: do you search for those cards, do you hold off of playing any oyher cards before going into Turret Mode (this is a complicated decision),  can you do more damage in Upgrade Mode (double EC can clear the board after a Force Deployment if Dawn flipping), will Recharge Mode gain you an advantage, when to use Adhesive, is there equipment destruction coming up that you have yo enter Upgrade Mode to prepare for, are you now the highest hp that Heavy Plating or  Recharge a mode can help you with damage mitigation. etc. There are ton of ingame decisions that often you don’t want to or have time ti get to that end point. As an example, you said that you only consider Gatling Gun If you have the cards, but you don’t consider the immediate damage or how many turns it will take you to eventualy overcome your total damage with Gatling Gun. Bunker’s biggest cincern is how many turns he has left, and you always have to consider that when dealing with the best poasible move.</p>\n<p>Also, I am not clear on what you mean when you say Omni or Maintenance for the other power. Unless you have an Aux Power Unit, Flak Cannon and Grenade Launcher will almost always be better and it is not worth wasting turns playing the other ones. For sure not Maintenance,  and so etimes Omni is worth of it you have Ammo Drop powering it, but it is very rarely worth it to play those before going into TM. Also, I very rarely go into TM with two power, the single extra damage on Flak Cannon is almost never worth stopping your deck.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:58:02.096Z",
