      {
        "id": 77137,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-15T02:01:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My whole point is that the endgame doesn't matter, it is how you get there. Every play with Bunker creates an incredible decision. While the end game might be the same, which can be said by many heroes, how you get there changes every game. You can argue that he always gets there the sam way, but I have very rarely seen that happen. Most of the time you are better off going into Recharge Mode with plating to get better stuff. At the very least you will get Auxillaru which will allow you to do damage and heal. If you don't have a target, then you should be building up for a massove turn. Yes, double mainframe has some uses, but 95% of the time there will be something better.</p><p>Edit: I am not saying you are wrong in your view, just that I view him very differently. If you are every interested in seeing how I play him, you can look at my guide. Bit it doesn't matter if you do, just enjoy the game.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:58:02.243Z",
